        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5b0746088fa72313783e3269",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2023-10-08T23:56:57.305Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "64eedae3d06dd309ae19ede4",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 2
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is a known Unity engine bug which affects some VR headsets, particularly Pimax and WMR.  The same bug affects several games.  As far as I know, Unity has never fixed it, and each game has had to apply what seems to be a fairly simple workaround to avoid the bug.  It has to do with a mode selection within Unity, and there's another mode which essentially works similarly but does not experience the bug.\n\nThis bug is only occurring in the VRChat Open Beta.  It is not occurring in the normal release version.\n\nHere's a Pimax forum post discussing the issue across several games:  https://community.openmr.com/t/unity-2020-bug-inaccurate-rotation-when-looking-around-other-incompatibilities/33934/44\n\nHere's the Unity bug that causes this discussed on the Unity forums.  This includes descriptions of how to workaround the bug:  https://forum.unity.com/threads/turning-issue-with-pimax-and-some-wmr-headsets.1205707/\n\nThis workaround needs to be implemented by the VRChat devs in order to resolve this issue.  The bug has already been present in Unity for years, and Unity can't be bothered to fix it, so don't hold your breath on that.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
